You are editing a C++17 repository (cwd is the repository root, a git worktree). You CANNOT run shell commands; use only your file read and file edit tools. Do not run git. Make exactly the change below and nothing else.

BACKGROUND: src/platform/system/UpdateService.cpp downloads an update asset (up to 512 MiB) with libcurl. It sets a 15 second TOTAL transfer timeout (CURLOPT_TIMEOUT_MS 15000L), so any slow connection fails the download. We want: no short total deadline, abort only when the transfer stalls, plus a generous hard cap.

STEPS
1. Read src/platform/system/UpdateService.cpp around line 825-870 (the function that sets up the asset download; it contains `curl_easy_setopt(request, CURLOPT_USERAGENT, "Inventatory updater");` followed by CURLOPT_CONNECTTIMEOUT_MS 5000L and CURLOPT_TIMEOUT_MS 15000L). There are TWO places that set CURLOPT_TIMEOUT_MS in the file: one with 8000L (a small metadata/API request, DO NOT touch it) and one with 15000L (the asset download, the one to change). Confirm which is which by reading the surrounding code before editing.
2. In the asset-download function ONLY, replace the single line
  curl_easy_setopt(request, CURLOPT_TIMEOUT_MS, 15000L);
with exactly these lines:
  // A large asset on a slow link must not hit a short total deadline; abort when the
  // transfer stalls (under 1 KiB/s for 30 s), with a generous hard cap of two hours.
  curl_easy_setopt(request, CURLOPT_LOW_SPEED_LIMIT, 1024L);
  curl_easy_setopt(request, CURLOPT_LOW_SPEED_TIME, 30L);
  curl_easy_setopt(request, CURLOPT_TIMEOUT_MS, 7200000L);
3. Re-read the edited region and confirm the 8000L line is unchanged and nothing else changed. Reply with a 3-line summary.
